  <h1>FTMO vs FundedNext: Full Comparison (2026)</h1>
  <div class="meta">By FundedEdge · 6 min read</div>

  <p>FTMO and FundedNext are two of the biggest prop firms in the industry — but they attract very different traders. FTMO is the industry standard. FundedNext is the new challenger with aggressive pricing.</p>

  <p>In this guide, we compare both side by side on the factors that actually matter: <strong>rules, pricing, profit splits, payouts, and account options.</strong></p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>💡 <strong>Quick verdict:</strong> Choose FTMO if you want maximum trust and industry-standard rules. Choose FundedNext if you want cheaper entry and fast payouts.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Side-by-side comparison</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Feature</th><th>FTMO</th><th>FundedNext</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Founded</td><td>2015 (Prague)</td><td>2022 (Dubai/UK)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Account sizes</td><td>$10K – $200K</td><td>$6K – $300K</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Starting price</td><td>From €89</td><td class="winner">From $59</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Profit target</td><td>10%</td><td class="winner">8% – 10%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Max drawdown</td><td>10%</td><td>10%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Daily drawdown</td><td>5%</td><td>5%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Profit split</td><td>80% – 90%</td><td class="winner">80% – 95%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Payout schedule</td><td>Bi-weekly</td><td class="winner">Bi-weekly + on-demand</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Platforms</td><td>MT4, MT5, cTrader, DXtrade</td><td>MT4, MT5, cTrader</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Rating</td><td class="winner">★ 4.9 / 5</td><td>★ 4.8 / 5</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Rules & difficulty</h2>

  <p>Both firms use a similar two-step evaluation model, but there are differences:</p>

  <h3>FTMO</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Two-step challenge:</strong> 10% target, then 5% target</li>
    <li><strong>Daily drawdown:</strong> 5% of initial balance</li>
    <li><strong>Max drawdown:</strong> 10% of initial balance (static)</li>
    <li><strong>No time limit</strong> — take as long as you need</li>
    <li><strong>News trading allowed</strong> on most accounts</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>FundedNext</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Multiple program types:</strong> Stellar 2-step, Express 1-step, Evaluation</li>
    <li><strong>Daily drawdown:</strong> 5% of initial balance</li>
    <li><strong>Max drawdown:</strong> 10% of initial balance (static)</li>
    <li><strong>Time limit:</strong> None on most programs</li>
    <li><strong>News trading allowed</strong> with conditions</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> FundedNext offers more program choices. FTMO's structure is more predictable for beginners.</p>

  <h2>Pricing</h2>

  <p>This is where FundedNext wins.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Account size</th><th>FTMO</th><th>FundedNext</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>$10K</td><td>€89 (~$97)</td><td class="winner">$59</td></tr>
      <tr><td>$25K</td><td>€179 (~$195)</td><td class="winner">$139</td></tr>
      <tr><td>$50K</td><td>€299 (~$326)</td><td class="winner">$239</td></tr>
      <tr><td>$100K</td><td>€449 (~$490)</td><td class="winner">$399</td></tr>
      <tr><td>$200K</td><td>€929 (~$1,014)</td><td class="winner">$759</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>FundedNext is consistently cheaper by 20-30% across all account sizes.</p>

  <h2>Profit splits & payouts</h2>

  <h3>FTMO</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Standard split:</strong> 80% to trader</li>
    <li><strong>Scaling plan:</strong> Increases to 90% after performance</li>
    <li><strong>First payout:</strong> Available after 14 days on funded account</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule:</strong> Bi-weekly</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>FundedNext</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Standard split:</strong> 80% to trader</li>
    <li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Up to 95% with performance</li>
    <li><strong>First payout:</strong> Available on-demand in some programs</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule:</strong> Bi-weekly, or on-demand depending on program</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> FundedNext edges ahead with the option for on-demand payouts and higher maximum split (95% vs 90%).</p>

  <h2>Trust & reputation</h2>

  <p>FTMO has been operating since 2015 and has paid out <strong>hundreds of millions</strong> to traders. Their reputation is unmatched in the industry.</p>

  <p>FundedNext launched in 2022 and has paid out over <strong>$100M</strong> already. Their reputation is strong but they haven't been around as long.</p>

  <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> FTMO wins on longevity. FundedNext wins on momentum.</p>

  <h2>Who should choose FTMO?</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>You want the most established, trusted firm</li>
    <li>You prefer straightforward rules (one program type)</li>
    <li>You don't mind paying a premium for peace of mind</li>
    <li>You're based in the EU (FTMO handles EU traders well)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who should choose FundedNext?</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>You want the lowest possible entry cost</li>
    <li>You want the highest possible profit split (up to 95%)</li>
    <li>You want flexible payout schedules (on-demand options)</li>
    <li>You're willing to trade with a newer firm for better terms</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="cta-block">
    <h3>Not sure yet?</h3>
    <p>Compare both firms side by side with all their details on FundedEdge.</p>
    <a href="../firms.html">View both firms →</a>
  </div>

  <h2>Final verdict</h2>

  <p><strong>FTMO</strong> is the safer choice. It's the industry standard, and it's what most professional prop traders use. If you can afford the higher entry price, go with FTMO.</p>

  <p><strong>FundedNext</strong> is the better value choice. Same rules, better pricing, higher potential split, and more payout options. If you're cost-conscious, go with FundedNext.</p>

  <p>Either way, both are legitimate firms with proven track records. You can't go wrong.</p>

